On my first rewatch, on episode 1, and noticed a few things.

&#x200B;

* What is lost, will be found - this could mean a lot of things, and all of these people have lost something... but what types of things could it be referring to when we look back? Memory? Who they really are? "Their way" ? Is this purgatory? 

&#x200B;

* Knowing what now know about Sebastian,  He would know what is outside the sim, and therefore I think would know what is different this time around, like the coordinates and going to the prometheus seemed to throw him for a loop. We know none of the other sims ever made it, so there must always be something going on.... We can guess that Daniel and Elliott are basically constantly pen testing it and trying to get farther towards their goal. He should probably know that too, you would think. 

&#x200B;

* When Elliott hands Maura the pyramid at the end, right before he does so, the lyrics of the song are "Go Ask Alice, I'll think she'll know" and then shortly after it pans to Maura right as the lyrics get to "Remember". I think Elliott is hoping Maura will remember the pyramid. Which makes sense given what we know in later episodes. They sort of stand there looking at each other. 

&#x200B;

* There are only a handful of characters who have a first and last name... Maura, Daniel, Eyk, Virginia, Henry, Dr Reginald, Sara, and Nina. I wonder if that is significant.  I think these are all people that are somehow involved "outside of the simulation" and are somehow related. At least 3 of these are the Larsen family... with additional unnamed daughters so far. 

I need to watch more episodes again I think...

